$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4b: After evaporation of the solvent (THF),
the residue was treated with diethyl ether and a saturated aqueous KF
solution. After vigorous stirring, FSnBu3 separated as a white solid. The
diethyl ether phase was separated, dried over MgSO4, and evaporated to
dryness. The residue was chromatographed (silica gel/ hexane) giving a
white solid, which was recrystallized from pentane at -28 °C. Isolation
of R2C6Cl2F3 from Catalytic Reaction Mixtures: R2= CH=CH2 (4a),
C6H4-4-OCH3 (4b). After evaporation of the solvent (THF), product 4a was
vacuum- distilled (70 °C, 3 mm) as a colorless liquid (80% isolated
yield). d 1.19. IR (NaCl) 2928 (m), 1610 (s), 1463 (vs), 1451 (vs), 1411
(vs), 1219 (s), 1081 (s), 991 (s), 936 (s), 860 (s), 801 (s); 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 6.61 (dd, 3,transJHH = 18.0 Hz, 3'cisJHH = 11.9 Hz, CHgem),
6.06 (d, 3,transJHH = 18.0 Hz, CHcis), 5.69 (d, 3'cisJHH = 11.9 Hz,
CHtrans); 13C{1H} NMR (CDCl3) δ 154.94 (ddd, 1JCF = 253.9 Hz, 4JCF = 9.2
Hz, 4JCF = 4.2 Hz, CF2), 153.77 (dt, 1JCF = 251.9 Hz, 4JCF = 5.5 Hz,
CF4), 123.22 (td, 4JCF = 7.9 Hz, 6JCF = 2.5 Hz, CH2), 121.60 (td, 3JCF =
17.3 Hz, 5JCF = 2.3 Hz, CH), 112.62 (td, 2JCF = 16.5 Hz, 4JCF = 4.6 Hz,
C-vinyl), 107.29 (ddd, 4JCF = 24.9 Hz, 2JCF = 21.0Hz, 4JCF = 3.9 Hz,
C-CF); 19F NMR (CDCl3/THF/ClPh) δ -115.41/-112.21/-111.50 (d, 4JFF = 2.4
Hz, 2F2), -113.29/-110.62/-109.57 (t, 4JFF = 2.4 Hz, F4); MS m/z (%) 226
(50) [M+], 191 (41), 156 (100), 105 (25). Anal. Calcd for C8H3Cl2F3: C,
42.33; H, 1.33. Found: C, 42.27; H, 1.32.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
