$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Stille Cross-Coupling Reaction Using Ligand 4
(Procedure B). In a glove box, the Schlenk tube equipped with a stir bar
was charged with Pd2(dba)3 (11.2 mg, 0.012 mmol, 1.5 mol %), CsF (272 mg,
1.8 mmol), and ligand 4 (11 mg, 0.025 mmol, 3.5 mol %). The tube was
fitted with a rubber septum and removed out of the glove box. One mL of
1,4-dioxane, aryl chloride (1.0 equiv, aryl chloride if solid was added
inside the glove box), and organotin reagent (1.1 equiv) were added
successively using syringes. The tube was sealed with a Teflon screwcap.
The reaction mixture was stirred for 30 minutes at room temperature then
heated with stirring at the indicated temperature for the indicated time.
The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, diluted with ether
or acetone, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel. Methyl
4-phenylbenzoate10 (Table 2, entry 1). Procedure B was followed using
methyl-4-chlorobenzoate (142 mg, 0.816 mmol) and phenyltributyltin (0.30
mL, 0.898 mmol). The reaction mixture was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (2% ethyl acetate/hexanes) to afford 164 mg
(95%) of the desired product as white solid. The 1H and 13C NMR spectra
were in accordance with those described in the literature.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly active palladium catalysts supported by bulky proazaphosphatrane
ligands for Stille cross-coupling: Coupling of aryl and vinyl chlorides,
room temperature coupling of aryl bromides, coupling of aryl triflates,
and synthesis of sterically hindered biaryls
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Su, Weiping; Urgaonkar, Sameer; McLaughlin, Patrick A.; Verkade, John G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2004), 126(50), 16433-16439

