$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3,5-Diphenyl-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (7a). Typical Stille procedure
(Table 2). To a stirred mixture of 3,5-dichloro-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one
(1) (50 mg, 0.273 mmol) and (Ph3P)2PdCl2 (9.6 mg, 0.0137 mmol) in MeCN (2
mL) at ca. 20 °C protected with a CaCl2 drying tube, tributylphenyltin
(220 mg, 0.60 mmol) was added. The mixture was then heated to ca. 100 °C
until no starting material remained (by TLC). The reaction mixture was
then cooled to ca. 20 °C and adsorbed onto silica. Dry flash
chromatography (hexane/DCM, 7:3) gave the title compound 7a (68 mg, 95%)
as yellow needles, identical to that described above.
3,5-Diphenyl-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (7a), yield (68 mg, 95%). mp
119-120 °C (from EtOH), Rf 0.49 (hexane/DCM, 1:1); (found: C, 67.7; H,
3.8; N, 10.4. C15H10N2OS requires C, 67.7; H, 3.8; N, 10.5%);
λmax(DCM)/nm 237 (log ε 3.06), 248 inf (3.01), 348 (3.28); νmax/cm-1
