$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 7-phenylsancycline 200mg of 7-iodosancycline
(0.37 mmol), 30 mg Pd(PPh3)2Cl2, 10mg AsPh3, and 6 mg of CuI is dissolved
in 25 ml of toluene with stirring. 0.050 ml of phenyl tri-n-butyltin is
added and the solution refluxed for 6 hours under nitrogen. The solution
is cooled to room temperature, filtered, the solvent removed and the
crude residue purified by preparative thin layer chromatography.
7-ethylenylsancycline, yield 94%. MS (FAB) 471 amu 1H NMR (Methanol d-4,
400MHz) δ 7.65 (d, J= 8.79Hz, 1H), 6.80 (d, J=8.76Hz, 1H), 5.56 (d,
J=18.42Hz, 1H), 5.25 (d, J=12.15Hz, 1H), 3.84 (s, 1H), 3.19 (m, 2H), 2.98
(s, 6H), 2.82 (m , 1H), 2.32 (m, 2H), 0.92 (m, 1H). IR(KBr) 3352, 3031,
2873, 2660, 1643, 1604, 1450, 1213, 978, 906, 888 cm-1. UV-Vis λ = 229,
255, 359 nm.
