$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ligand 1b: 2-bromopyridine (1.48 g, 0.89 mL,
9.4 mmol), 2-methyl-5-(tributylstannyl)thiophene (4.0 g, 10.3 mmol),
Pd(PPh3)4 (0.54 g, 0.47 mmol) and CsF (3.12 g, 20.6 mmol) were weighed
into a Schlenk tube and 60 mL of dioxane was added. The reaction mixture
was sparged for 15 minutes with argon. The reaction mixture was heated at
100 °C for 36 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled down and was passed
through a silica gel plug to remove the solids. The silica plug was
eluted with 250 mL of ethyl acetate. The combined organic fractions were
evaporated to yield an oily residue, which was chromatographed on silica
gel with dichloromethane/hexane (2:1 v/v) as the eluent to yield 1.59 g
(97%) of 1b as a white solid. Ligand 1c: The experimental procedure was
the same as for 1b. 2–bromopyridine (1.63 g, 0.98 mL, 10. mmol),
2-methoxy-5-(tributylstannyl)thiophene (6.0 g, 15 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.60
g, 0.51 mmol), CsF (3.4 g, 23 mmol). Yield was 1.82 g (93%) using
DCM/hexane (2:1 v/v) as the eluent. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.51 (d,
1H), 7.63 (t, 1H), 7.55 (d, 1H), 7.26 (d, 1H), 7.08 (t, 1H), 6.24 (s,
1H), 3.97 (s, 2H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 168.7, 153.1, 149.5, 136.5,
130.8, 122.9, 121.1, 117.6, 105.2, 60.3. HRMS calc. for C10H10NOS (M)+,
192.0478; found, 192.0478. mp = 45-46 °C.
