$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3,5-Diphenyl-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (7a).
Typical Stille procedure (Table 2). To a stirred mixture of
3,5-dichloro-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (1) (50 mg, 0.273 mmol) and
(Ph3P)2PdCl2 (9.6 mg, 0.0137 mmol) in MeCN (2 mL) at ca. 20 °C protected
with a CaCl2 drying tube, tributylphenyltin (220 mg, 0.60 mmol) was
added. The mixture was then heated to ca. 100 °C until no starting
material remained (by TLC). The reaction mixture was then cooled to ca.
20 °C and adsorbed onto silica. Dry flash chromatography (hexane/DCM,
7:3) gave the title compound 7a (68 mg, 95%) as yellow needles, identical
to that described above. 3,5-Di(fur-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (7n).
Similar treatment of of 3,5-dichloro-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (1) (50
mg, 0.273 mmol) with 2-(tributylstannyl)furan (224 mg, 0.60 mmol) gave
the title compound 7n (61 mg, 92%) as yellow needles. mp 167-168 °C
(cyclohexane); Rf 0.30 (hexane/DCM, 7:3); (found: C, 53.6; H, 2.5; N,
11.5. C11H6N2O3S requires C, 53.7; H, 2.5; N, 11.4%); λmax(DCM)/nm 250
(log ε 3.14), 288 (2.70), 319 inf (2.89), 329 (2.96), 381 (3.53), 394
(3.53), 415 (3.48); νmax/cm-1 3165w, 3132w, 3115w, 1628s, 1560m, 1483s,
1439w, 1400m, 1350w, 1306w, 1287m, 1223w, 1213w, 1200w, 1165w, 1142w,
1082w, 1045s, 1016s, 997m, 918w, 883s, 866m, 835m, 785s, 773s; δH(500
MHz; CDCl3) 7.88 (2H, d, J 3.5, furyl H), 7.68 (2H, br s, furyl H), 6.62
(2H, dd, J 3.3, 1.3, furyl H); δC(125 MHz; CDCl3) 159.9 (s), 149.7 (s),
147.7 (s), 146.3 (d), 119.9 (d), 112.8 (d); m/z (EI) 246 (M+, 82%), 125
(100), 97 (14), 93 (16), 70 (13), 64 (10), 51 (4).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium Catalyzed C-C Coupling Reactions of
